hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1675","Narrated to us al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān, who said: al-Shāfiʿī said: Mālik informed us.\n\nAlso narrated to us Yūnus ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, who said: Ibn Wahb informed us, that Mālik informed him, from Makhzūma ibn Sulaymān, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās (RA), that he informed him:\n\nThat he spent the night as a guest with Maymūna, the Mother of the Believers (RA), who was his maternal aunt. I reclined across the width of the pillow, while the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) and his family reclined along its length. He (ﷺ) then slept until half the night had passed, or shortly before or after that. He (ﷺ) then awoke, sat up, and wiped his face with his hand. He then recited the last ten verses of Sūrat Āl ʿImrān. He then stood up to a hanging water skin, performed ablution from it, and did so excellently. He then stood to pray.\n\nIbn ʿAbbās (RA) said: So I stood beside him. The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) placed his right hand on my head, took hold of my right ear, twisted it gently, and prayed two rakʿahs, then two more light rakʿahs. He then left and prayed the dawn prayer.\n\nCHAPTER:"
